# Review package: ticket 07, 346cc58..bb2659c

## Commits
### bb2659c
fix(state): run push and pop native on the raw receiver

The direct push and pop wrappers took the direct path when the raw
array target was the receiver, because its [HOOKS] slot carries the
same context as the Proxy. That made push.call(raw, x) call hooks and
wake subscribers, unlike the other five wrappers and unlike a direct
write on the raw object, which never enter the traps (Q71 b).

Fall through to the native method when the receiver is the context's
own target, keep the native TypeError for a nullish receiver, flip the
test that pinned the old behavior and fix the wording in src/AGENTS.md.

